{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.dd1_degree_of_doubling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.dd1_degree_of_doubling","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L95-L104","doc":"**(CONDITIONAL on the conjecture.)**  If a Vassiliev-degree function realises the\ndoubling, then at every `A ≥ 2` its degree is `2(A−1)` and strictly exceeds the naive\nMilnor degree `A−1`.  Fully verified modulo the single open class instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.BarSymmetricDegreeDoubling.first_surviving_is_doubled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.BarSymmetricDegreeDoubling.first_surviving_is_doubled","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The first non-vanishing degree is the bar-symmetric doubled order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.BarSymmetricDegreeDoubling.linear_milnor_part_absent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.BarSymmetricDegreeDoubling.linear_milnor_part_absent","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The linear Milnor-degree part carries no deficit weight (cyclic-trace\nannihilation, #4480): the realised degree is never the bare `A−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.BarSymmetricDegreeDoubling.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.BarSymmetricDegreeDoubling.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.BarSymmetricDegreeDoubling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.BarSymmetricDegreeDoubling","kind":"class","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L83-L93","doc":"**(CONJECTURE, primary — OPEN.)**  A Vassiliev-degree function `vdeg` on the\nBrunnian deficit family realises DD-1: the linear (degree-`A−1`) part vanishes and\nthe first non-vanishing degree is the doubled `2(A−1)`.  Content-bearing; NO instance\n(the honest open state).  Do not fabricate an instance — that would launder the\nbridge (§\"Axiomatization is NOT a Proof\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.doubling_A6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.doubling_A6","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L71-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.doubling_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.doubling_A3","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L68-L70","doc":"Sanity anchors: A=3 → 4 = 2·2; A=6 → 10 = 2·5 (the #4480 endpoints). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.qou_order_is_double_milnor_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.qou_order_is_double_milnor_degree","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L60-L66","doc":"**The factor-of-2 discrepancy, exactly.**  The qou deficit's leading Vassiliev\ndegree is exactly **twice** the length-`A` Milnor invariant's Vassiliev degree.  So\nthe Milnor-Vassiliev bridge, invoked at face value (first non-vanishing Vassiliev\ninvariant = `μ̄` at degree `A−1`), does **not** predict the observed order — a real\ngap, not a rescaling artifact (§1 pinned the variables). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.qouDeficitLeadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.qouDeficitLeadingOrder","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The qou Brunnian deficit's leading order (proved lower bound #4471; measured\nexact #4480): `2(A − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.milnorVassilievDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.milnorVassilievDegree","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L52-L54","doc":"Vassiliev degree of the length-`A` Milnor invariant `μ̄(12…A)` (cited:\nBar-Natan 1995 / Lin): `A − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.grading_change_fixes_origin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.grading_change_fixes_origin","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L40-L48","doc":"**`sinh` vanishes at `0`, so the change of variable fixes the origin.**  With\n`Real.sinh_zero`, `2·sinh 0 = 0`: the substitution `q = e^{ℏ}` sends `ℏ = 0` (i.e.\n`q = 1`) to `h = 0`.  Together with `deficit_var_eq_two_sinh`, `h = 2 sinh ℏ =\n2ℏ + O(ℏ³)`, so `h` and `ℏ` share the same leading order (the harmless factor `2` is\na unit): an order-`k`-in-`h` term is an order-`k`-in-`ℏ` (Vassiliev-degree-`k`) term.\nThe `2(A−1)` deficit order is therefore a genuine Vassiliev **degree** statement, not\na variable-convention artifact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.deficit_var_eq_two_sinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorVassilievGrading.deficit_var_eq_two_sinh","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorVassilievGrading.lean#L31-L38","doc":"**The deficit variable is `2·sinh` of the Vassiliev variable.**  With `h = q−q⁻¹`\n(the qou Markov-deficit variable) and `ℏ = log q` (`q = e^{ℏ}`, the finite-type\nvariable), `h = 2·sinh ℏ`.  Hence the two gradings differ by no rescaling constant\nother than the harmless factor `2`: they assign the **same leading order** to a term. ","signatureChunk":0}]}